      "notes": [
        "internal/proxy/admin_dataworks.go:353 parseExpiryHorizon multiplies the day/week count by the unit without an overflow guard, so an absurd value such as ?expiring_within=200000d wraps int64 to a negative duration and is returned with ok=true. The deadline then lands in the past and the endpoint answers with an empty/incorrect expiring set instead of the 400 the doc comment promises for non-positive windows. Only reachable with unrealistic admin input, so low impact, but it contradicts the stated contract.",
        "internal/proxy/admin_dataworks.go:288 and internal/proxy/admin_ui.go:14575 verified: entitlementExpiresWithin uses Before(deadline) while entitlementExpired uses Before(now) and the inactive branch continues, so no entitlement is counted in both inactive_access and expiring_access; the admin tab sum is therefore correct.",
        "web/src/pages/secondary/secondary-pages.tsx:199 the typeMap completion (low_fit_scores, inactive_access, retirement_candidates) is a separate pre-existing bug fixed alongside the feature. It is small, correct against the action types emitted in admin_dataworks.go, and called out in the commit message, so not treated as scope creep.",
        "web/src/pages/secondary/secondary-pages.tsx:364 the governance card labelled 사용 권한 (비활성 또는 만료) still shows only summary.inactive_access, while the legacy admin UI now shows inactive_access + expiring_access. The number stays accurate for its label, but the two UIs report different totals for access problems.",
        "The response gained a top-level expiring_within field that is not declared in web/src/types/dataworks.ts ActionCenterResponse; harmless today since nothing reads it, worth adding if the SPA exposes the window later.",
        "Tests do exercise the change: TestDataWorksActionCenterWarnsBeforeEntitlementExpires asserts summary.expiring_access==1 / entitlement_expiring action and the 13w vs 7d windows, all of which fail on main (the counter and the query param do not exist there). Verified locally: go vet, full go test ./... , web tsc -b and vitest all pass.",
        "Working tree carries an unrelated uncommitted deletion of web/dist/.gitkeep; it is not part of main...HEAD, but it should not be committed with this change.",
        "No migrations, no auth/permission/billing/deletion logic touched (the window parse happens after requireAdminAuthorization), and no external state is written, so the change is a clean revert."
      ],
